# What a `p.demo(...)` leaves behind. The compile demos in lectures/1-intro
# build in place, on purpose -- the point of the page is that you can look at
# the .i, the .s and the .o afterwards -- so the products are ignored and the
# sources beside them are not.
lectures/*/examples/*.i
lectures/*/examples/*.s
lectures/*/examples/*.o
lectures/*/examples/mini_ollama
lectures/*/examples/cpp_demo
